11896	{"artifactId":"HLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c","entry":{"id":"migrated-HLD-2ff0dfdadb1c8d1c-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-07T08:41:32.484Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"pass","summary":"review: pass","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.epic","stage":"design.epic","verdict":"pass","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s1–s5 acceptance criterion in DEF-2ff0dfda is designed, and no non-goal (UI, writes, push, new state machine, migration) is built.","evidence":"DEF.md §6 lists s1 ac1-6, s2 ac1-7, s3 ac1-7, s4 ac1-5, s5 ac1-6. The HLD's §6 boundaries map each of these to the owning story's LLD tests. Specific coverage: s4 ac2 through s1 sourcing story membership from accepted EXT records; s5 ac3 through workflow.deliveryEvidence; s3 ac7 through the confirmed q17f993e9 policy. The design adds no write path, no push channel and no UI, and it states that stage is a display projection, which matches DEF §3 non-goals. [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Unresolved references count toward Needs attention (S003:FR005), and resolved or overridden blocks are excluded.","evidence":"In sc3, 'unresolved-parent' is fixed at attention:true. In sc5, blocking = effectiveVerdict==='block' AND unapproved AND no override, which matches DEF S003:FR005 and ac5/ac6. [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"workflow.pending treats an absent store as an empty success, an unreadable store as { error }, and skips one malformed file. The daemon wires it as a lazy-import handler-map entry.","evidence":"In pending.ts:108, `if (!existsSync(dir)) return [];`. Lines :76-80 map a throw to `{ error: 'workflow.pending: ...' }`. Lines :120-122 skip a malformed file. In daemon/index.ts:686-688, `'workflow.pending': async (params) => { const { handleWorkflowPending } = await import('../workflow/pending.js'); ...process.env['INSRC_REPO']`. [files: src/workflow/pending.ts, src/daemon/index.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"AMD records are flat ({ id, epicHash, amendment, status, proposedAt, approvedAt?, rejectedAt? }), while other kinds are { meta, body }.","evidence":"AMD-761a43a6fa645815-2.json has top-level id, epicHash, amendment{type,storyId}, proposedAt, status:'approved' and approvedAt. amendments/store.ts:112-140 writes status/approvedAt/rejectedAt at the top level. EXT-761a43a6fa645815-s10.json is { meta, body }. [files: src/workflow/amendments/store.ts, .insrc/artifacts/AMD-761a43a6fa645815-2.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"A standalone BUILD records a story-level result as body.tasks[].id equal to the story id. The ISSUE's fix BUILD carries the issue hash in meta.epicHash, and ISSUE meta carries issueHash, magnitude and a self-slug parentRef.","evidence":"BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1.json has meta {standalone:true, sizeClass:'trivial', epicHash:'0855311b6b32eb72', storyId:'S001', approvedAt} and body.tasks [{id:'S001', passed:false}]. ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72.json has meta issueHash '0855311b6b32eb72', magnitude 'small', epicSlug 'bug-build-record-triage-routed-small' and parentRef {slug:'bug-build-record-triage-routed-small'}, which is the issue's own slug. [files: .insrc/artifacts/BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1.json, .insrc/artifacts/ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The reused identity helpers exist with the stated shape: storyIdToOrdinal accepts s1/S1/S001, taskIdToOrdinal accepts only t<n>, deriveWorkItemIdentity(hash, createdAt, storyId?), and workItemAnchorCreatedAt = epicCreatedAt ?? createdAt at storage.ts:181.","evidence":"In id.ts:123, `/^[sS](\\d+)$/`. In id.ts:133, `/^t(\\d+)$/` throws otherwise, so a BUILD task id 'S001' cannot mint a task (consistent with the HLD rule). id.ts:202-216 returns {canonical, slug, epicSegment, story?}. storage.ts:181-182 returns `meta.epicCreatedAt ?? meta.createdAt`. [files: src/workflow/id.ts, src/workflow/storage.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"effectiveReviewVerdict(review, reviewResolutions) in review/resolve.ts is the existing 'still blocking' rule, and computeHldEffectiveHash is a pure helper reusable without the amendments listers.","evidence":"resolve.ts:57-64 returns 'block' while any HIGH/MED finding lacks a resolution, else 'pass'. The same rule gates approval in gates.ts:581 and drives artifact-content.ts:186. computeHldEffectiveHash is exported from artifacts/lld.ts:221 and called purely in staleness.ts:69 with (baseHld.meta.runId, amendments.map(a=>a.id)). [files: src/workflow/review/resolve.ts, src/workflow/gates.ts, src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The new types are named with a Delivery prefix because path-scheme.ts already exports ArtifactKind and WorkItemKind with different members.","evidence":"path-scheme.ts:46 has `ArtifactKind = 'SPEC'|'DEF'|'HLD'|'LLD'|'PLAN'|'BUILD'|'CR'|'EXT'|'ISSUE'` (no AMD), and :50 has `WorkItemKind = 'epic'|'standalone'`. shared/artifacts.ts:31 also exports an ArtifactKind. A Delivery prefix avoids all three collisions. [files: src/workflow/path-scheme.ts, src/shared/artifacts.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The deliveryEvidence id pattern ^(SPEC|DEF|HLD|LLD|PLAN|BUILD|CR|ISSUE|EXT|AMD)-[0-9a-f]{16}(-[A-Za-z0-9]+)?$ admits every real artifact file stem and the per-kind id minters.","evidence":"storage.ts:148-175 mints DEF-/HLD-/SPEC-/ISSUE-<hash> and LLD-/PLAN-/BUILD-/CR-<hash>-<storyId>. amendments/store.ts mints AMD-<hash>-<n>. A glob for files under .insrc/artifacts that are not one of these ten kinds returned none. Observed stems such as BUILD-…-s10, CR-…-S001, EXT-…-s10 and AMD-…-2 all match the suffix class. [files: src/workflow/storage.ts, src/workflow/amendments/store.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Staleness hashes the approved amendments in rising approvedAt order, as the existing scanner does.","evidence":"In amendments/store.ts:212-218, listApprovedAmendments filters status==='approved' and sorts by `(a.approvedAt ?? '').localeCompare(b.approvedAt ?? '')`. In staleness.ts:68-69, `computeHldEffectiveHash(baseHld.meta.runId, amendments.map(a => a.id))` is computed over that list. [files: src/workflow/amendments/store.ts, src/workflow/amendments/staleness.ts]","action":"None. Note that sc6's presentation sort by amendmentId is a string sort ('AMD-x-10' < 'AMD-x-2'), while listAmendments sorts numerically (store.ts:207). Still deterministic, but consider sorting numerically for display.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Older or variant records are lifted correctly: meta.seededFromSpec holds the bare spec hash, and CR records carry meta.reviewedBy only when stamped.","evidence":"In artifacts/lld.ts:339-340 and define.ts:113-114, the renderer prints `SPEC-${seededFromSpec}`, so the stored value is the bare hash. code-review/types.ts:180 has `reviewedBy?: 'controller'|'daemon'`, and runner.ts:274 writes it only when given. CR-972bf31d13c81a2f-s1.json has no reviewedBy. The HLD's `reviewedBy: ... | null` handles both. [files: src/workflow/artifacts/lld.ts, src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, .insrc/artifacts/CR-972bf31d13c81a2f-s1.json]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Moving the build-without-plan half of s4 ac4 into s5 does not redesign another story's contract. It needs s2's route (sc4), which s4 cannot read on its parallel branch.","evidence":"DEF s4 ac4 ('a story with a build record but no plan … marked as having incomplete evidence') is route-dependent: the small route needs no plan (s2 ac2). The HLD has s4 test the no-title half, and has s5 own the route-aware check and its test. Both use the sc3 'incomplete-evidence' code that s1 owns, so no contract owned by another story is altered. [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md]","action":"None. Make sure s4's and s5's LLDs both record this split so neither drops it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Evidence reads cannot escape the store, and rendered markdown is read only under the existing docs/ containment rule with realpath re-checks.","evidence":"artifact-content.ts:116-147 does a lexical relative() check against docs/, then realpathSync on both sides and re-checks containment before reading. The HLD keeps the same pattern for the artifact store: an id-pattern check, then a join under ARTIFACTS_DIR, then a realpath that must stay inside the store. It also defines distinct { error } results for invalid and unknown ids. [files: src/workflow/artifact-content.ts]","action":"None.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each story's acceptance criteria map to a named test in its LLD, including the regression check that workflow.pending and workflow.artifactContent tests pass unchanged.","evidence":"HLD §6 requires each story's LLD to map: s1 ac1-6, s2 ac1-7, s3 ac1-7, s4 ac1-5 and s5 ac1-6. These counts match DEF §6. It names concrete fixtures from real records, which I verified exist: BUILD-0855311b6b32eb72-s1, ISSUE-0855311b6b32eb72 and BUILD-d88062a6e63aa312-s1. handleWorkflowPending and handleArtifactContent are extracted pure functions that can be tested without the daemon (pending.ts:60-66, artifact-content.ts:95-100). [files: docs/epics/e1-delivery-read-model-daemon-from-E202610072ff0dfda/DEF.md, src/workflow/pending.ts, src/workflow/artifact-content.ts]","action":"None. One gap: DEF s4 ac3 asks the notice to name 'the coverage it leaves unknown', and sc3's record-unreadable notice carries only fileNames and a message. State in s1's or s4's LLD what that message must say, and assert it.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-07T08:41:32.484Z","model":"cli-claude:opus","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
